Manual review corrections for this page's first pass.

- "assuming a is non-zero" and "given that $a>1$ and a is an integer."
  left the variable "a" as bare prose outside math mode even though the
  same sentences use "$a$" elsewhere; wrapped both in math mode.
- "approximate the x-value" left the variable "x" as bare prose;
  changed to "approximate the $x$-value", matching the repo's
  $x$-axis/$x$-value convention.
- The two piecewise functions in the "critical points, maxima, and
  minima for the following piecewise functions" group used a raw
  "\{\begin{matrix}...\end{matrix}" construct: a lone "\{" left
  unmatched by any closing brace, so the piecewise definition rendered
  without its enclosing bracket. Changed both to
  "\begin{cases}...\end{cases}" with a "\text{if }" condition label on
  each branch, matching the piecewise-function convention already used
  elsewhere in the repo (e.g. vol2-3-7-improper-integrals.tex and
  vol3-4-2-limits-and-continuity.tex).

